      "rationale": "Reviewed pinned checkout/setup-node, dependency-free Node governance tests and validators, their static imports and policy/profile inputs. Contract tests use temporary fixture directories and a short-lived local port probe, never an application build/server. npm run skills:check --ignore-scripts suppresses npm pre/post hooks; npm ci --ignore-scripts plus npm audit retain dependency scanning without package build hooks. Pinned TruffleHog scans Git history with prebuilt tooling; pinned Semgrep installs scanner tooling and scans src/worker/tests only. No application, container-image, browser or performance build/test is reachable. Full application suites remain local and must be recorded separately. Issue 42 package.json review: the sole addition is the manually invoked pointview:setup command; neither workflow nor any CI npm command calls it, and no lifecycle hook or existing command changed. Pipeliner refresh review: new lifecycle, paired-QA, cycle and Showcase modules are pure decision/validation helpers; Project and home commands are read-only and are not invoked by CI. Updated tests exercise temporary adoption previews and link validation only. New recursive reference validation reads static Markdown/HTML, covered here. No workflow action, package dependency, setup hook or application command changed. Question update: reviewed the bounded pure matcher, exact Builder clause exception, profile propagation, YAML/provider scans and temporary installer fixtures with cleanup. No new command execution, application builds, dependencies or workflow changes. Conflicting text blocks even matching reconciliation hashes; destination bytes are rechecked before apply.",
